  "response_text": "Since the type of stack the STM32F401RE has is a full, descending stack, the memory allocated for the stack is at the ending address of the RAM\u2019s memory. Say the MSP_init_val is 0x20018000. A descending stack will grow downwards, i.e. go towards 0x00. Therefore, the new value for the PSP is size of the MSP stack subtracted from the MSP_Init_val. This will give the PSP stack a starting address (in hexadecimal) that is smaller than the MSP stack\u2019s starting address due to the descending nature of the stack (with a 0x400 difference in memory between them). Since the memory allocation for the stack is built from the RAM\u2019s \u201cending\u201d memory address, it is therefore necessary to know what that \u201cending\u201d memory address is to add to the stack, and this memory address is the MSP_init_val.\\n",
